---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageIntro from "../components/PageIntro.astro";
import ScreenshotFigure from "../components/ScreenshotFigure.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy-first meeting status | Meeting Pulse"
  description="A small macOS app that lets your loved ones see if you're in a meeting, without showing them your meeting. Here's what the app sees and shares."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="Privacy"
    title="The viewer gets a signal, not a window into the meeting."
    description="Meeting Pulse needs permission to detect a supported state on the owner’s Mac. The public surface is intentionally much smaller."
  >
    <div class="button-row" style="margin-top: var(--space-lg)">
      <a class="button button--accent" href="/docs/accessibility-permission/">Why permission?</a>
      <a class="button" href="/open-source/">Inspect the project</a>
    </div>
  </PageIntro>

  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="dark-panel">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The boundary</p>
        <h2>Permission for the owner app. Restraint for the viewer.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          The owner app can inspect supported app state through macOS
          Accessibility APIs. The viewer only needs to know whether to call.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="boundary-list">
        <li><span>Meeting titles and URLs are not shown to viewers.</span></li>
        <li><span>Participants, audio, video, screenshots, OCR, and screen contents are not uploaded.</span></li>
        <li><span>Meeting Pulse does not require a browser extension, Slack bot, OAuth, or calendar access.</span></li>
        <li><span>When the product cannot trust a state, it displays unavailable.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="split-section">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">What permission does</p>
        <h2>It lets Station look for supported call states.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="split-section__body">
        <ScreenshotFigure
          light="/images/product-screens/meeting-pulse-station-privacy-light.jpg"
          dark="/images/product-screens/meeting-pulse-station-privacy-dark.jpg"
          alt="Meeting Pulse Station privacy settings"
          caption="Privacy settings are visible from Station."
        />
        <p>
          macOS protects Accessibility access because it can expose information
          on a computer. Meeting Pulse asks for that access for a narrow reason:
          to detect the supported meeting state the owner wants to share.
        </p>
        <p>
          Read the repository and the project’s security guidance before
          installing. If the product changes its data boundary, the public
          explanation should change with it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">What the viewer can know</p>
      <h2>Small enough to understand at a glance.</h2>
    </div>
    <ul class="checklist">
      <li><span>In a meeting</span></li>
      <li><span>In a meeting, but it’s fine to ring through</span></li>
      <li><span>Meeting status unavailable</span></li>
      <li><span>Not connected</span></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
